.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/out/
# Stale build outputs left by earlier previsualisation passes.  `desktop/out/`
# above only covers the canonical directory, so these were being picked up by
# `git add -A` and would have shipped ~10 MB of dead bundles.
desktop/out.*/
desktop/npm-install.*.log
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.data/*
# ...but the deterministic audit-simulation fixtures are test *inputs*,
# not runtime state: ~12 small files that several suites read from
# `.data/audit-sim/`.  Leaving them untracked meant a fresh clone, CI, or
# another machine failed with FileNotFoundError on ledger.csv.  Note the
# pattern is `.data/*` rather than `.data/` — git cannot re-include a path
# whose parent directory is excluded outright.
!.data/audit-sim/
.env
*.log
# ...but the logs under a *deliverable* archive are the artifact itself, not
# runtime noise.  Without these negations `*.log` above silently excluded the
# three most important files of the run archive — including the main timeline
# log — so the archive would have been committed without its centrepiece.
!docs/全流程运行日志-20260912/**/*.log
!docs/AI组网Demo-20260911-原始数据/**/*.log
coverage.xml
.coverage
cankao/
# TypeScript incremental build state (regenerated on every typecheck).
*.tsbuildinfo
# One-off local database probes at the repo root.  Not part of the project;
# `_m7_check.py` even says "run once, delete later" in its own docstring.
_conn_check.py
_m7_check.py
# A literal directory named "%SystemDrive%" gets created when a script using
# %VAR% is run from a shell that does not expand it (Git Bash).  It ends up
# holding copies of Windows' own ProgramData caches, which must never be
# committed.  Junk — safe to delete, but ignored so it cannot leak in.
%SystemDrive%/
# A stray duplicate of the run archive appeared on disk during the CI work
# (1712 files, created 14:47 on 2026-09-12); its origin is not accounted for.
# It is NOT deleted — the retention rule is "keep everything" — but it must not
# be committed.  Verified 2026-09-22: its file list is identical to
# `审计项目案例报告效果展示/全流程运行日志-20260912/` (1712 entries) and the
# sampled files are byte-for-byte identical (`00-归档说明/README.md` =
# f2889003…, `校验清单-sha256.csv` = d12bfb00…, `01-输入数据/audit-sim/ledger.csv`
# = 79a9c4f0…), so committing it doubles that archive in git.
#
# This rule used to read `docs/全流程运行日志-20260912-完整归档/`, which matched
# nothing: the copy actually lives under `审计项目案例报告效果展示/` and nests a
# second directory of the same name inside it.  The rule never took effect and
# all 1709 files were tracked — twice over.  `git rm -r --cached` removed the
# redundant copy from the index; the files stay on disk.
审计项目案例报告效果展示/全流程运行日志-20260912-完整归档/
# IDE state.  Nothing here is needed to build or run the project, and the
# per-user files (misc.xml, modules.xml) only describe one machine's checkout.
# `git rm -r --cached .idea` removed the already-tracked copies; the files stay
# on disk.
.idea/
